    {
      "v": 1,
      "zh": "你们拈阄分地为业，要献上一分给耶和华为圣供地，长二万五千肘，宽一万肘。这分以内，四围都为圣地。",
      "en": "“‘When you allot the land as an inheritance, you will offer an allotment[NOTE:1] to the Lord, a holy portion from the land; the length will be 8¼ miles[NOTE:2] and the width 3⅓ miles.[NOTE:3] This entire area will be holy.[NOTE:4]",
      "notes": [
        "Heb “a contribution.”",
        "Heb “25,000 cubits” (i.e., 13.125 kilometers). The measuring units here are the Hebrew “long” cubit, consisting of a cubit (about 18 inches or 45 cm) and a handbreadth (about 3 inches or 7.5 cm), for a total of 21 inches (52.5 cm). Because modern readers are not familiar with the cubit as a unit of measurement, and due to the additional complication of the “long” cubit as opposed to the regular cubit, all measurements have been converted to American standard miles (one mile = 5,280 feet), with the Hebrew measurements and the metric equivalents given in the notes.",
        "The LXX reads “20,000 cubits.”tn Heb “10,000 cubits” (i.e., 5.25 kilometers).",
        "Heb “holy it is in all its territory round about.”"
      ],
